# Rank 1150 / CVE-2026-25083: GROWI's OpenAI thread and message routes look
# up a ThreadRelation by threadId alone, so a logged-in user who learns a
# shared AI assistant's thread id can read or post into another user's
# thread (CWE-862). postMessageHandlersFactory and its siblings
# (get-messages, get-threads, delete-thread, edit) call
#
#   const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({ threadId });
#
# with threadId taken straight from req.body/req.params and no filter tying
# the row to req.user. The fixed revision adds userId: user._id to every
# ThreadRelationModel query and to getThreadsByAiAssistantId's and
# deleteThread's signatures.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. Scanning either revision reports the same seven
# VYQL-CFG-014 rows plus one VYQL-RF-003 row, all in unrelated login and
# page-listing code; req.body is labelled code.HttpInput at the threadId
# destructure but ThreadRelationModel.findOne itself carries no sink or
# check label in either revision. code.IdorPolicyReview (VYQL-AUTH-081) is
# the right concept and has JavaScript bindings, but every one of them keys
# on a presence match naming one project's identifiers (a Prisma
# accounts.update call missing "currentUserId", a phpReview marker string),
# not on the general shape "a query object literal missing an ownership
# key". Stating that shape as a binding without naming this project's
# userId/ThreadRelationModel needs the engine to reason about which fields
# an object literal omits relative to a schema it has never seen, and a
# flat-bag negation of that kind reports a collection lookup that
# legitimately owns every row it returns: an identical shape. No definition
# change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions rejected.

test "rank1150: thread lookup keyed only by threadId, no owner filter"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-AUTH-081
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  export const postMessageHandlersFactory = (crowi) => {
    return [
      loginRequiredStrictly,
      certifyAiService,
      async (req, res) => {
        const { user } = req;
        const { aiAssistantId, threadId } = req.body;

        const aiAssistant = await AiAssistantModel.findById(aiAssistantId);
        if (aiAssistant == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('AI assistant not found'), 404);
        }

        const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({ threadId });
        if (threadRelation == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('ThreadRelation not found'), 404);
        }

        return streamMessageToThread(threadRelation, user);
      },
    ];
  };
  ```

test "rank1150: thread lookup scoped to the requesting user's id"
  lang javascript
  reject VYQL-AUTH-081
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  export const postMessageHandlersFactory = (crowi) => {
    return [
      loginRequiredStrictly,
      certifyAiService,
      async (req, res) => {
        const { user } = req;
        const { aiAssistantId, threadId } = req.body;

        const aiAssistant = await AiAssistantModel.findById(aiAssistantId);
        if (aiAssistant == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('AI assistant not found'), 404);
        }

        const threadRelation = await ThreadRelationModel.findOne({
          threadId,
          userId: user._id,
        });
        if (threadRelation == null) {
          return res.apiv3Err(new ErrorV3('ThreadRelation not found'), 404);
        }

        return streamMessageToThread(threadRelation, user);
      },
    ];
  };
  ```
